WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.299 --> 00:00:08.099
When I was very young like around 13
years old I used to travel

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:10.600
to San Diego and Los Angeles.

00:00:10.613 --> 00:00:15.009
And I realized and I noticed there that the air pollution was

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:19.050
horrendous at the time. And I thought well why should people live like this?

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:25.090
So I learned about climate and air
pollution in more detail.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.480
And then I just dedicated my career so this is what I want to do. I want to understand

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.619
and solve large-scale problems of air pollution and climate.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.800
For the last 20 years I've been looking at both the problems and the solutions.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.900
But even the last five years

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.000
it's been more focus on the solutions because we really need to solve the problems at this point.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.000
With this course,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.230
we'll learn how it's possible to solve these major problems that have not been solved before

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.620
including air pollution which kills
seven million people per year.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.980
We'll learn how to eliminate air pollution
entirely from the face of the earth.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:01.690
We'll learn how to eliminate the
emissions associated with global warming,

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:07.270
which will eventually result in
temperatures stabilizing and coming back

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:12.759
to pre-industrial time temperatures of
the earth. And we will eliminate global

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:18.189
insecurities of energy resources which
arise due to the limited availability of

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:22.800
fossil fuels and their decreasing
availability over time.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.399
So those who are

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:28.539
interested in transitioning - those
companies, those individuals, and also

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:34.770
policymakers who want to pass laws - to
try to effect a transition not only

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.399
cost-effectively but also equitably,
would be interested in taking this course.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:45.969
So students in this course will
not only learn the details about what's

00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:51.310
needed to go to 100% clean renewable
energy. But they will also be given

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.770
information about what policies are
available to do this, and and what's been

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:02.349
done so far. You know the bottom line is
we need to combine ... since we're

00:02:02.349 --> 00:02:06.340
electrifying all energy sectors we're
really a combining electricity, heating,

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:11.680
cooling, industry, transportation - we're
electrifying those sectors.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.750
And we can use a combination of not only
renewable resources, but electricity storage,

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:22.150
heat storage, cold storage, some
hydrogen storage, also what's called

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:27.819
demand response. These techniques and
technologies are discussed in this

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:32.260
course and basically how to keep the
grid stable is something that hopefully

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:36.220
you'll be more confident about after
taking the class.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.540
This skill is very

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:44.170
important today because there are many
jobs that require an understanding of a

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:48.690
clean renewable energy system. There are over 200 companies in the world

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.269
including 8 out of the 10 biggest
companies of the world that have

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:56.560
committed to 100% clean renewable energy. Who is going to guide these companies

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.599
I'm optimistic we can solve these
problems. And actually having changed my

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:08.079
own life by building a completely
renewable home with no gas. Just uses

00:03:08.079 --> 00:03:13.239
electricity with heat pumps, induction
cooktop stove, electric cars, and

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:17.859
generates more electricity than it uses
in the annual average. I know that it's

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:23.349
possible not only do this on a local
scale but also on a large scale. And this

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:27.819
is maybe passionate since I feel like I
understand the issues quite well now. I

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:33.669
feel like the solutions are also at our
at hand. And so it's very important to

00:03:33.669 --> 00:03:37.870
provide that information to others to
help solve this large-scale problem that

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.590
affects humanity.

